# Keep the build context to source only. Everything below is either
# regenerable, local-only, or irrelevant to `go build`, and shipping it would
# slow the build and widen the set of bytes the daemon has to look at.
.git
.github
.agent-artifacts
docs
deploy
# The only two directories the image copies from the repository are cmd/,
# internal/, sql/ and the demo tree below, and Docker's ignore rules are
# last-match-wins: a path that has to stay in the context needs its parents
# re-included first.
#
# The demo tree the Go web tier renders at runtime with LOLSTATS_AGG_FIXTURES=only
# (see the Dockerfile) lives at fixtures/site since 2026-09-17, when the retired
# Astro tree that used to carry it was deleted. `fixtures` is ignored as a whole
# because the hand-authored Riot payloads under it are tests' input, not the
# image's, and the two lines below put the demo tree back.
fixtures
!fixtures/site
!fixtures/site/**
# The checked-in Data Dragon projection the tier reads when LOLSTATS_DATA_DIR
# points at it. It is not copied into the image (the projection the image needs
# is embedded in the binary, internal/webtier/data.go), and it is large. The
# upstream-shaped payloads the crawler tests read are a different tree, at
# fixtures/ddragon/, and are excluded with the rest of fixtures/.
projection
# The generated artifact shape cmd/gen-types writes. internal/aggmodel owns the
# document and the image emits it from there, so the copy on disk is a
# reviewer's and a test's input rather than the image's.
schema
*.md
bin
node_modules

# Secrets never enter a build context, even though nothing here copies them.
.env
*.pem
*.key
